{"path":"std/fs/fn.rename.html","title":"Function rename","description":"Renames a file or directory to a new name, replacing the original file if to already exists.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function rename"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#2770-2772","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub fn rename<P: AsRef<Path>, Q: AsRef<Path>>(from: P, to: Q) -> Result<()>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Renames a file or directory to a new name, replacing the original file if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" already exists."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will not work if the new name is on a different mount point."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"platform-specific-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform-specific behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function currently corresponds to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"rename"},{"type":"text","value":" function on Unix and the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"MoveFileExW"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"SetFileInformationByHandle"},{"type":"text","value":" function on Windows."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because of this, the behavior when both "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" exist differs. On Unix, if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" is a directory, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" must also be an (empty) directory. If "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a directory, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" must also be not a directory. The behavior on Windows is the same on Windows 10 1607 and higher if "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"FileRenameInfoEx"},{"type":"text","value":" is supported by the filesystem; otherwise, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" can be anything, but "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" must "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be a directory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that, this "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/index.html#platform-specific-behavior","title":"mod std::io","children":[{"type":"text","value":"may change in the future"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will return an error in the following situations, but is not limited to just these cases:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" does not exist."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The user lacks permissions to view contents."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"from"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"to"},{"type":"text","value":" are on separate filesystems."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    fs::rename(\"a.txt\", \"b.txt\")?; // Rename a.txt to b.txt\n    Ok(())\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Ause+std::fs;%0A%0Afn+main()+-%3E+std::io::Result%3C()%3E+%7B%0A++++fs::rename(%22a.txt%22,+%22b.txt%22)?;+//+Rename+a.txt+to+b.txt%0A++++Ok(())%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]}]}}
